-Dense Copy Extraction extracts a spatial region defined by a bounding box from a sparse grid representation into a contiguous dense 3D array [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of converting sparse, hierarchical data structures (like OpenVDB) into uniform grids suitable for dense rendering, machine learning inputs, or standard image processing [S1, S2, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that query individual points or gradients, this method performs a bulk conversion, initializing the output with a background value and overwriting it with interpolated values for all coordinates within the specified bounds [S1, unofficial].
