 ## Background
-Dense Copy Extraction is a standard operation in volume rendering and scientific visualization, particularly when working with sparse data structures like OpenVDB [S1, S2, unofficial]. It allows for the conversion of hierarchical, sparse data into a uniform grid format that is easier to process with standard image processing libraries or rendering engines [S1, S2, unofficial]. The method is commonly used in applications such as fluid simulation, SDF rendering, and medical imaging [S1, S2, unofficial].
